{# ── FAQ ── #}
<section class="bg-cloud">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:720px;">
    <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
    <h2>Common questions about YouTuber taxes</h2>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do I have to pay taxes on YouTube AdSense income?</summary>
      <p>Yes. AdSense income is taxable self-employment income. Google will send you a 1099-MISC if you earn $600 or more, but you're technically required to report all income regardless. I make sure it's all handled correctly on your return.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can I deduct my camera, microphone, and equipment?</summary>
      <p>Yes — equipment used for your YouTube business is a legitimate business expense. This includes cameras, lenses, microphones, lighting, tripods, gimbals, hard drives, and more. The deduction depends on how the equipment is used and how it's categorized.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What if I only make a small amount from YouTube?</summary>
      <p>Even a small amount of YouTube income is taxable and needs to be reported. The good news is that if you also have expenses, those can offset your income and reduce what you owe. Don't ignore small amounts — they add up and so do the deductions.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do I need to pay quarterly estimated taxes?</summary>
      <p>If your YouTube income is significant enough that you'll owe $1,000 or more in taxes for the year, the IRS generally expects you to make quarterly estimated payments. I help you figure out whether you need to do this and how much to pay each quarter.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can I deduct my home office or editing space?</summary>
      <p>If you use a dedicated space in your home exclusively for creating content, you may be able to claim a home office deduction. It has to be a regular and exclusive use space — a corner of your living room doesn't count, but a dedicated studio room does.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
